{"name":"City Lights","hex":"#dfe6ea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"city lights","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The aggregate of street lights of a city, particularly at night (often referring to the exciting attractions that the city features, especially its nightlife)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city_lights"}],"entries":[{"title":"City Lights (band)","blocks":[{"text":"City Lights was an American pop punk band from Columbus, Ohio, formed in 2008 by Zachary LeCompte-Goble and Hartley Lewis. They released two EPs and two studio albums during their six-year tenure; the latest being The Way Things Should Be, released on December 10, 2013, via InVogue Records. The band signed to InVogue in May 2011. The band announced their dissolution on February 13, 2014. One year later on February 13, 2015, they released a third EP titled Acoustic EP 2. They announced that they had no intention of getting back together but if schedules permitted they would still take part in shows and put out music."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_Lights_(band)"},{"title":"City Lights (Dr. John album)","blocks":[{"text":"City Lights is an album by Dr. John, his first for Horizon Records. It was released in 1978."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/68/Dr_john_-_city_lights.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_Lights_(Dr._John_album)"},{"title":"City Lights","blocks":[{"text":"City Lights is a 1931 American synchronized sound romantic comedy-drama film written, produced, directed by, and starring Charlie Chaplin. While the film has no audible dialog, it was released with a synchronized musical score with sound effects. The story follows the misadventures of Chaplin's Tramp as he falls in love with a blind woman and develops a turbulent friendship with an alcoholic millionaire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/City_Lights_%281931_theatrical_poster_-_retouched%29.jpg/330px-City_Lights_%281931_theatrical_poster_-_retouched%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_Lights"},{"title":"City Lights (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"City Lights is the debut extended play by South Korean singer Baekhyun. It was released on July 10, 2019 by SM Entertainment. The album features six tracks, including the lead single \"UN Village\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Baekhyun_-_City_Lights.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_Lights_(EP)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/City_Lights_promo_still.jpg/500px-City_Lights_promo_still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/City_Lights_promo_still.jpg/1280px-City_Lights_promo_still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/City_Lights_promo_still.jpg/500px-City_Lights_promo_still.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Tramp meets the Blind Flower Girl and falls in love.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACity_Lights_promo_still.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Albert_Einstein_and_Charlie_Chaplin_City_Lights_premiere_1931.jpg/500px-Albert_Einstein_and_Charlie_Chaplin_City_Lights_premiere_1931.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Albert_Einstein_and_Charlie_Chaplin_City_Lights_premiere_1931.jpg/1280px-Albert_Einstein_and_Charlie_Chaplin_City_Lights_premiere_1931.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars